WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:08.040
Hi, my name is Kheira Bey and I am a professional
actress living and workin in London and the

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.740
United Kingdom.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:15.129
Today I have had the pleasure of training
at really amazing establishments such as the

00:00:15.129 --> 00:00:19.550
Royal Academy of Dramatic Art and the Sylvia
Young Theatre School.

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:24.210
And I’ve also had the pleasure of selling
out really amazing theaters in London such

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:28.180
as the Kingshead Theatre, Alcoa Theatre and
Pleasant’s Theatre.

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:33.640
And so today I am going to be providing general
advice to other actors about how to learn

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:39.530
lines really quickly, how to choose your maybe
first headshot photographer, and also how

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:42.730
to earn more money to facilitate your acting
career.

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.780
3 Tips for Memorizing Lines

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:51.530
Firstly, I know that learning lines is probably
the most boring and possibly even stressful

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:53.239
part of an actor’s job.

00:00:53.239 --> 00:00:58.970
Especially when you have less than 24 hours
to learn a script or in my case I know I have

00:00:58.970 --> 00:01:06.250
had to learn 18 pages of dialogue and I was
given the script at 8:00 p.m. in the evening

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:11.159
and then had to audition at 7:00 a.m. the
next morning in a Persian accent and I didn’t

00:01:11.159 --> 00:01:13.310
even know what a Persian accent was.

00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:14.680
And I had to learn how to do it.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:21.220
So yeah I think generally there is some ways
that I know I do in order to help learn lines

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:24.510
really quickly and efficiently.

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:31.549
So firstly, I think actors should always be
reading whether this is books, plays, magazines,

00:01:31.549 --> 00:01:37.580
newspaper articles (you know the free newspaper
in the troupe) just because every time you

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:42.680
do that you are really strengthening the muscles
up here because you are retaining all of that

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:45.140
information in such a condensed amount.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:49.750
So then when you are actually faced with a
script (a whole new piece of text) those muscles

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:51.960
are stronger and more stimulated.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:57.080
So it’s kind of easier to absorb those lines
more quickly.

00:01:57.080 --> 00:02:05.600
And also the second part of reading for character
preparation, I will read everything in order

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:08.229
to get in character for a role.

00:02:08.229 --> 00:02:16.220
This might be radio pieces, recounts, diary
entries (if I’m doing something really historical)

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:18.010
or anything really?

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:27.090
Like at the moment in my room at home I have
fashion magazines from Russia (like replica

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:32.270
ones) because I was trying to get into character
for a Russian girl like last week.

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:37.510
So I have that and if you’re more engaged
with the kind of world you’re trying to

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:44.489
create the lines kind of sink in a bit easier
because you’re owning them in your own way

00:02:44.489 --> 00:02:47.930
and you’re just more connected to them.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:54.910
The last way I like to learn lines is by focusing
on movement memory and muscle memory and kind

00:02:54.910 --> 00:03:02.360
of trying to challenge myself to kind of think
how many ways I can learn my lines and get

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:08.010
that into my body so it can be by whispering
them, shouting them, singing them, writing

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:15.560
them all the way out, doing them in as many
accents as I can and doing them as if I’m

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:21.200
talking to a child or like a really, really
old person just so that I am getting really

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.200
into my body.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:28.200
So that my body will know how to do the lines
when my mind forgets or I’m really tired

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:29.470
and can’t forget.

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:33.950
4 Tips On Finding The Right Headshot Photographer

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:36.480
Next I’m going to be talking about headshots.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:41.280
So headshots are like this size [motions in
a frame around face] and they are really important

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:43.180
because they get you in the room.

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:47.599
So first piece of advice like I understand
they are really expensive for what they probably

00:03:47.599 --> 00:03:52.030
are, but do not scrimp on headshots.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:56.849
And so when you are going about photographers
just remember that the casting director or

00:03:56.849 --> 00:04:04.599
director, producer or whoever will be casting
from about a hundred thumbnail images all

00:04:04.599 --> 00:04:06.659
tiled on a computer screen.

00:04:06.659 --> 00:04:12.250
So if your headshot doesn’t have your eyes
sticking out on top of them and you know they

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:16.250
can have a massive screen full of so many
people, I mean you’re probably not going

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:21.269
to get called in, sorry.

00:04:21.269 --> 00:04:26.479
And also secondly when you are choosing your
headshot photographer please remember to exhaust

00:04:26.479 --> 00:04:29.039
all of your research methods.

00:04:29.039 --> 00:04:36.379
Don’t just Google ‘Headshot Photographer’
and then whatever your city or town is because

00:04:36.379 --> 00:04:41.979
chances are…yeah…that might be good but
why don’t you actually go on an agency website

00:04:41.979 --> 00:04:43.990
of actors who are actually booking jobs.

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:49.130
Have a look at their headshots and are they
interesting, are they engaging, do you want

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:50.779
to put them in a room?

00:04:50.779 --> 00:04:58.159
Then probably save that, save all of the names
of the people that interest you and choose

00:04:58.159 --> 00:05:01.240
whoever you want really.

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:06.240
Next I am going to talk about when I go into
a headshot photographer’s website.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:10.580
Okay, they might have loads of famous people
they’ve taken pictures of which is great.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:14.240
They are going to have them first because
it obviously looks great for them.

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:20.419
But did the famous people actually look like
you because remember that when you’re purchasing

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:23.399
headshots you don’t know in advance what
they are going to look like so you’ve got

00:05:23.399 --> 00:05:28.550
to really estimate what you might end up with
at the end of the day.

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:34.870
So if I’m looking at a website and I see
loads of male actors that are really famous

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:39.050
and standing out, I’m probably going to
be a bit like “Well, I don’t really see

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:48.909
females so I can’t really estimate how myself
could be interpreted as so just bear that

00:05:48.909 --> 00:05:49.909
in mind.

00:05:49.909 --> 00:05:56.330
Bear in mind that a fashion photographer is
amazingly different from a headshot photographer.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:06:01.349
So you’re not a model, you are an actor
during the day, just bear that in mind when

00:06:01.349 --> 00:06:03.240
you’re choosing your headshot photographer.

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:08.189
Ways To Earn Money While Pursuing An Acting
Career

00:06:08.189 --> 00:06:12.300
Lastly, if you’re young in your career (like
perhaps me) and you’re thinking “How on

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:17.289
earth am I going to afford all these amazing
headshots to get really amazing auditions

00:06:17.289 --> 00:06:19.240
to also learn lines for?”

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:24.400
I have some money advice for you because we
all need to do something I think on the side.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:29.729
So you probably have a job already but that
doesn’t stretch to extra classes, extra

00:06:29.729 --> 00:06:36.280
plays, trips to Russia to get into character
or Russian museums to get into character.

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:46.360
So firstly I want you to kind of think about
doing something like writing or freelance

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:52.259
writing or blogging because a lot of actors
currently do this and they have blogs where

00:06:52.259 --> 00:06:57.289
they tell people about what they do and also
share their skills and also expertise in their

00:06:57.289 --> 00:07:03.490
field but a lot of actors don’t actually
use Google Adsense or a similar kind of system

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:08.470
to put adverts on their sites and make more
money out of it that way.

00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:11.909
So I guess that’s something to kind of think
about because that’s free money and you’re

00:07:11.909 --> 00:07:17.990
not really doing anything in order to get
the money so just think about it that way.

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:22.110
Also I know that quite a lot of actors share
skills.

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:29.279
So it can be teaching, that can be…I like
to run workshops for little kids.

00:07:29.279 --> 00:07:30.770
Like I get paid to do that.

00:07:30.770 --> 00:07:35.340
For me that’s just fun because I don’t
really think of it as a job, I just get to

00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:40.149
just hang around and play games with kids
and watch them act, which is really, really

00:07:40.149 --> 00:07:41.149
fun.

00:07:41.149 --> 00:07:48.979
And also I know actors that share whatever
skills they have so accents, languages, musical

00:07:48.979 --> 00:07:55.979
instrument skills practically anything and
you can also work whenever you want, flexible

00:07:55.979 --> 00:08:01.349
hours which is great when you’ve kind of
got auditions, rehearsals, classes, filming

00:08:01.349 --> 00:08:02.349
all of that.

00:08:02.349 --> 00:08:05.099
You can just earn money when you can.

00:08:05.099 --> 00:08:09.449
And lastly, I just want you to kind of think
about that you can practically do anything

00:08:09.449 --> 00:08:16.050
for money, so you could be a hair model, you
could drive for Uber, you could be a delivery

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:21.550
driver, you could be one of those people who
literally get paid to take documents from

00:08:21.550 --> 00:08:25.089
one building to another, there are so many
different ways.

00:08:25.089 --> 00:08:28.749
And really just research and have fun with
it.

